 "about": "Michael's severity calls on reviewed Clawd builds, as (build, view, region, severity) labels for calibrating charkit.perceptual, and his before/after calls as pairs. Severity: 0 praised ('huge improvement', 'much better'; 'relative': praise of a change, not a clean bill), 1 mild ('questionable', 'slightly'), 2 moderate (a named fault, not called severe), 3 severe ('catastrophically off', 'very obviously visually glitched', 'serious', 'most severe', every flag of 2026-09-29). view '*': the flag names no view; the metric takes the worst of the views it measures. 'who': michael (his words on that build; the default), inferred (his flag, the build or the region read by the integrator), agent (found by a workstream's measure, not called by him): the michael-only variant drops the others. 'check': what the geometric QA said of the same thing on that build (its own qa/qa.json, the QA of the time); 'check_now': the check added after the flag to catch it, as measured later on that build (from the workstream notes). Pairs: 'kind' praise (his before/after call), implicit (a flag he stopped making after the fix, while reviewing that build), unreviewed (a fix confirmed only by the checks); each pair's 'check' is the geometric check on both builds.",
 "scale": {"0": "praised", "1": "mild", "2": "moderate", "3": "severe"},
